{
  "enabled": true,
  "name": "TDD Gate (red-green-refactor)",
  "description": "Manually run before/while implementing a unit of behaviour to enforce the red -> green -> refactor discipline and the definition of done.",
  "version": "1",
  "when": {
    "type": "userTriggered",
    "patterns": []
  },
  "then": {
    "type": "askAgent",
    "prompt": "Act as a TDD gate for the change currently in progress, per the tdd steering. Verify and report on:\n1. RED: was a failing test written first (or alongside) that states the desired behaviour, and did it fail for the correct reason before implementation? If we cannot show a red step, note it.\n2. GREEN: does the implementation make the test pass with the minimum necessary code (no speculative/unused abstraction)?\n3. REFACTOR: is the code clean with the test still green?\n4. Co-location: tests sit next to source (foo.test.ts / Foo.test.tsx), no *.only or skipped tests committed.\n5. Boundaries + error paths covered; property tests present and tagged where the input space is large (>=100 runs).\n6. Definition of done: run `npx vitest run` and `npx tsc --noEmit` in the affected package(s) and confirm both are green/clean.\nOutput a PASS/FAIL checklist. For each FAIL, give the smallest next action to get to green. Keep it concise."
  }
}
